    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912163649576099~1/edit": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Occupational Therapy)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Department: Occupational Therapy (Melbourne) Location: VIC Campus Location: Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV102103#098 Make significant contributions to development, implementation and evaluation of Bachelor of Occupational Therapy course Work alongside motivated colleagues within a highly recognised, innovative national school ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Part time 21 hours/week, continuing opportunity working at Melbourne campus About the role: Operating within Occupational Therapy (Melbourne) , the Lecturer (Occupational Therapy) makes significant contributions to the development, implementation, evaluation and continuous improvement of the Bachelor of Occupational Therapy course at ACU by contributing to excellence in teaching, learning, curriculum development and undertaking quality research. Supported by an established local and national academic team, the position will consult with the Deputy Head of School, Head of Discipline and Course Coordinators and other university staff as required to ensure implementation of courses, support students to achieve their academic goals and advance the standing of the Occupational Therapy program nationally. Experience in mental health settings and/or professional practice interest and experience is highly desirable. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Tammy Boatman, Deputy Head of School Allied Health (VIC) - National School of Allied Health at: Tammy.Boatman@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $142,635 - $168,287 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $120,529 - $142,305 (pro rata) pa (Academic Level B), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 25-OCT-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. This position requires a Working with Children Check (WWCC) and/or Working with Vulnerable People Check (WWVP) (ACT only). Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912176516891299~1/edit": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Student Wellbeing",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Department: Student Experience Directorate Location: NSW,QLD,VIC Provide strategic leadership across our student wellbeing portfolio nationally Support student flourishing academically, personally and socially ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, senior manager role (five years), based at our Brisbane, North Sydney or Melbourne campus We are seeking an accomplished and values-led senior leader to provide strategic leadership across our nationally delivered student wellbeing portfolio. Reporting to the Director, Student Experience and Enhancement, the Associate Director, Student Wellbeing will play a pivotal role in shaping an integrated, evidence-informed and student-centred approach to wellbeing, safety and support across ACU's campuses. This is a significant leadership opportunity to strengthen the quality, consistency and impact of services that support students to flourish academically, personally and socially. The role leads a diverse portfolio including counselling, medical centres, access and disability, student accommodation, safeguarding, student care, gender-based violence prevention and response, and related wellbeing services. The successful candidate will lead National Managers and multidisciplinary professional teams, provide senior advice on student wellbeing risks and service performance, and drive the implementation of ACU's university-wide Student Wellbeing Framework. You will ensure services are clinically governed, compliant, inclusive, risk-informed and aligned with ACU's Mission, Vision 2033 and commitment to whole-person education. Key priorities include: Leading the development and delivery of integrated, nationally consistent student wellbeing services. Providing strategic leadership across clinical governance, professional standards, safeguarding, accessibility, student safety and regulatory compliance. Embedding evidence-informed approaches to measuring student wellbeing, evaluating service effectiveness and improving outcomes. Building a collaborative, high-performing and student-centred culture across multidisciplinary teams. Partnering across the university and with external stakeholders to strengthen support pathways, risk management and service innovation. We are seeking a senior leader with substantial experience in a large and complex organisation, ideally with experience leading multidisciplinary wellbeing, health, clinical, care or support services. You will bring strong judgement, high-level stakeholder skills and demonstrated capability in service integration, governance, risk management, continuous improvement and leading through complexity. A postgraduate qualification in a relevant discipline is required, and a clinical or regulated professional background will be highly regarded. At ACU, our Mission informs everything we do. We are committed to fostering thriving communities, respecting the dignity of the human person, and supporting students to succeed through compassionate, ethical and high-quality services. This role offers the opportunity to make a meaningful contribution to the wellbeing, safety and success of students across a national university community. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to John Burdick, Director, Student Experience and Enhancement at: john.burdick@acu.edu.au How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Candidate Information Package and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process. Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 25-OCT-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912178685905399~1/edit": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Theology)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Department: National School of Theology Location: NSW Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Strathfield, Australia Job No: APTAV129377#021 Deliver excellence in teaching and learning in Catholic social thought and Catholic theology ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, continuing role based at our North Sydney or Strathfield campus with some hybrid flexibility About the role: As a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Theology, you will contribute academic expertise to the School of Theology, Faculty of Theology and Philosophy, to ensure excellence in teaching and learning in Catholic social thought and Catholic theology, while undertaking and leading research in the field. You will also contribute to the mission of the school, faculty and university through teaching, research, academic administration, curriculum development, program coordination and work collaboratively across the university and with external partners. The preferred candidate will need to be willing to apply for a Mandatum to teach in Theology and Religious Education disciplines per the requirements of Ex Corde Ecclesiae. An interest in and ability to teach into the women's leadership for mission program is desirable. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Belinda Malone, Executive Officer, Faculty of Theology & Philosophy at: Belinda.Malone@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $142,635 - $168,287 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $120,529 - $142,305 (pro rata) pa (Academic Level B), OR $178,482 - $193,772 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $151,018 - $164,087 (pro rata) pa (Academic Level C), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 25-OCT-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912162643825099~1/edit": {
      "title": "Director, Global Operations",
      "description": "Closing Date: 06/11/2026 Department: Global Location: NSW,VIC Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV122004#005 Help shape ACU's next phase of international engagement Bring institutional expertise together to deliver on global ambition Full-time, fixed-term (5 year) appointment Based at ACU's North Sydney or Melbourne campus Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a public institution grounded in Catholic tradition, dedicated to academic excellence, human dignity and the common good. With campuses across Australia, a campus in Rome , the Human Flourishing Centre in Indonesia , and an expanding online presence. Guided by Vision 2033 , ACU combines a strong Australian presence with an increasingly connected international footprint. Reporting to the Pro-Vice-Chancellor Global, the Director, Global Operations offers an opportunity to shape how ACU delivers its next phase of international engagement under Vision 2033. Working across faculties and professional portfolios, the Director will turn global strategy into tangible outcomes, from new education partnerships to the development of ACU's offshore activities, while building the models and institutional capability that enable lasting success. A collaborator and integrator, the Director will bring together faculties, professional portfolios and Global teams to deliver shared priorities. The role will connect international initiatives with the University's academic and professional expertise, establish clear responsibilities and strengthen planning, governance, resourcing and performance arrangements across organisational boundaries. Working with academic and professional leaders, the Director will establish and manage the operational arrangements supporting major Global initiatives, including transnational education, international partnerships, the Rome campus, the Human Flourishing Centre and other offshore activities. The role will manage implementation plans and dependencies, resolve barriers to delivery and ensure appropriate oversight of financial, regulatory, operational and reputational risk within its remit. The role may also include responsibility for developing selected international relationships or markets, with scope and priorities agreed with the Pro-Vice-Chancellor Global. Working closely with relevant Global leads, faculties and professional portfolios, the Director will progress opportunities from initial engagement through to implementation. As a key member of the Global leadership team, the Director will provide trusted advice to the Pro-Vice-Chancellor Global and exercise sound judgement about priorities, resources and emerging risks. Success will require the ability to build productive relationships, secure decisions and sustain delivery through competing demands and changing external conditions. ACU is seeking an accomplished leader with a demonstrated record of implementing strategy, shaping operating models and delivering complex initiatives across organisational boundaries. The successful candidate will combine strategic thinking with commercial and financial acumen, strong governance and risk judgement, and a practical approach to building institutional capability. Experience in international education, transnational education or global partnerships will be highly regarded. Candidates may bring relevant experience from higher education or another large, complex organisation with an international remit. A collaborative leadership style, the ability to build shared ownership and a record of leading change will be central to the appointment. ACU has partnered with Kuras Leadership Search for the recruitment of this position. For a confidential discussion or to request a copy of the Candidate Information Pack, please contact Betty Kuras on +61 3 9653 9599 or via email at apply@kurasleadershipsearch.com, quoting job code 2688. Applications close Friday, 6 November 2026. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912157477159499~1/edit": {
      "title": "Campus Facilities Manager (North Sydney)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Department: Facilities Management North Sydney Location: NSW Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia Job No: APTAV104102#003 Opportunity to manage campus facility operations, operational workflows, contractor performance and stakeholder engagement Lead a supportive, high performing team delivering safe and efficient facilities management services ACU offers 17% superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, permanent opportunity working at North Sydney campus About the role: Operating within Facilities Management (North Sydney) , the Campus Facilities Manager (North Sydney) provides leadership of campus facilities operations through effective management of people, budgets, operational workflows, contractor services and stakeholder relationships. Working at ACU's North Sydney site, the Campus Facilities Manager will lead the Facilities Services Officers and Administrators, develop staff capability, deliver high quality efficient services, manage contractor performance, drive continuous improvement and ensure resources are aligned with operational standards, compliance practices, customer service outcomes and the university's operational priorities. The position oversees day to day campus operations including planning, scheduling and coordination of property related services, maintenance activities and projects, regular inspections, built environment assessments and operating systems including building management systems, and coordinates appropriate rectification to support campus safety, compliance and business continuity. Other responsibilities include contributing to the standardisation and continuous improvement of facilities management practices and supporting the effective deployment of resources across the campus in response to changing operational requirements. The role also builds and maintains productive relationships with university staff, internal and external stakeholders, contractors and service providers. The Campus Facilities Manager will need to be contactable outside normal working hours in the event of an emergency or situation of immediate risk to students, staff or university property. If attendance on campus or remote management of an incident is required outside of working hours overtime provisions may apply in accordance with the ACU Enterprise Agreement. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Neil Hodgson, National Manager - Facilities Management Operations at: neil.hodgson@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $138,111 - $154,409 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $116,706 - $130,478 (pro rata) pa (HEW 8), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 27-OCT-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912156587782999~1/edit": {
      "title": "Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander Curriculum & Pedagogy Coord",
      "description": "Closing Date: 28/10/2026 Department: Social Work (Canberra) Location: ACT,NSW Campus Location: Canberra, Australia | North Sydney, Australia | Strathfield, Australia Job No: APTAV102103#097 Provide academic and cultural leadership to prepare graduates for culturally safe, responsive practice with indigenous peoples and communities Lead integration of Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander ways of Knowing, Doing and Being into Social Work programs ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous parental, carers and study leave provisions Full time, continuing opportunity with hybrid flexibility working at North Sydney, Strathfield or Canberra campus About the role: Operating within Social Work (Canberra) , the Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander Curriculum & Pedagogy Coordinator, a teaching focussed position, provides academic and cultural leadership to prepare ACU Social Work and Speech Pathology graduates for culturally safe, responsive practice with Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples and communities. The position leads the integration and continuous improvement of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander ways of Knowing, Doing and Being across curriculum, pedagogy, assessment and professional practice education with opportunities to influence broader Allied Health initiatives over time. The Senior Lecturer supports the development of graduates to meet the ethical, professional and accreditation expectations of their disciplines and contributes to the ongoing quality of professional practice. A key focus of the role will be to strengthen the cultural capability of staff through mentoring, professional development, resource development and curriculum consultation enabling academic teams to confidently embed Indigenous perspectives throughout the student learning journey. Work collaboratively with discipline leaders, academic staff, students, elders, communities and professional and health bodies to ensure curriculum is culturally responsive, respectful and aligned with contemporary best practice and accreditation expectations. Build staff capability and capacity to develop culturally aware graduates who will positively impact health and social service delivery. Develop partnerships with Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander elders, communities and stakeholders to advance culturally responsive education and community engaged learning. Embed culturally driven learning outcomes whilst considering social, physical, spiritual and emotional health and wellbeing of cultures throughout the lifespan in line with the Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Health Curriculum Framework. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Elspeth Froude, National Head of School - National School of Allied Health at: Elspeth.Froude@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $178,482 - $193,772 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $151,018 - $164,087 (pro rata) pa (Academic Level C), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 28-OCT-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. This position requires a Working with Children Check (WWCC) and/or Working with Vulnerable People Check (WWVP) (ACT only). Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) ACU considers that being Aboriginal or a Torres Strait Islander is a genuine occupational requirement for this position under s 42 of the Discrimination Act 1991 (ACT)/ s 14 of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1977 (NSW), s 25 of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Qld)/ sub-s 56(2) of the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA)/ sub-s 26(3) or s 28 of the Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic). Candidates are encouraged to visit our Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Peoples Employment webpage for valuable resources to assist them in their application, including the Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Candidate Job Guide . Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912161561907999~1/edit": {
      "title": "Executive Dean of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Department: Faculty of Health Sciences Location: NSW,QLD,VIC Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Brisbane, Australia | Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV101331#081 Lead a multi-campus faculty at Australia's leading Catholic university preparing the health workforce of the future Full-time, fixed-term (5 year) appointment Based at ACU's Melbourne, North Sydney or Brisbane campus About ACU: As one of the top ten Catholic universities worldwide, ACU is clear about its Catholic identity and mission within the Catholic intellectual tradition. Central to this is ACU's commitment to truly student-centred education; research that is impactful, engaging, and responsive to society's rapidly changing needs; and a strong, vibrant, and sustainable university culture. ACU is a young university making a significant impact. Ranked in the top 100 young universities globally and a leader in employability with 95 per cent of graduates employed, the university has seven campuses across Australia, with its global reach complemented by ACU Online, more than 200 partner universities, and its campus in Rome, Italy. About the Position: The Faculty of Health Sciences teaches and researches across nursing, midwifery, paramedicine, physiotherapy, occupational therapy, speech pathology, psychology, social work, exercise science, nutrition, biomedical science and public health. It is organised into three schools: Allied Health; Behavioural and Health Sciences; and Nursing, Midwifery and Paramedicine. The faculty's research is internationally recognised. ACU ranks first worldwide for research quality in psychology (Times Higher Education), in the top 15 for nursing and 17th for sport science (Shanghai Ranking). It also has strengths in cardiovascular disease and metabolism, health services research, recovery and rehabilitation, and mental health. Reporting to the Provost, the Executive Dean provides academic leadership and operational management and chairs the faculty board. The faculty's leadership team includes a Deputy Dean, an Associate Dean Learning, Teaching and Professional Experiences, and an Associate Dean Research. Key responsibilities include setting goals in line with the ACU Strategic Plan and Innovation Strategy, course development and review, and academic governance consistent with TEQSA and the Higher Education Standards Framework. The Executive Dean also drives new approaches to professional experience and clinical placements and, working with the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research and Enterprise), builds on this research record. Externally, the Executive Dean leads the university's relationships with Catholic hospitals and other health industry partners, and with Catholic universities around the world. Internally, the role manages the faculty budget, develops new revenue sources and builds a caring community among staff and students. The Successful Candidate: The successful candidate will bring: A PhD in a health sciences discipline and a record of impact in teaching and learning, research, professional practice and community engagement Knowledge of the Catholic health sector and its governance; A strong grasp of the Australian tertiary sector, with the ability to interpret policy and academic regulation and to influence policy development; Proven ability to lead change in a large, complex organisation; Demonstrated success converting opportunities into new research and education outcomes, including course and program design; Sound financial management, including budgets and the deployment of people and resources; Experience building partnerships and commercial agreements in Australia and internationally. Most importantly, the new Executive Dean will demonstrate a genuine commitment to ACU's mission and values, and the confidence to connect the faculty's work to them. Devereaux Consulting is supporting ACU with the search for the university's next Executive Dean, Faculty of Health Sciences. For a confidential conversation or to request further information, please contact Dr Jackie Besley, Managing Partner, Devereaux Consulting on +61 413 633 195 or email ExecDeanHealth@devereauxconsulting.com. The closing date for applications is: Monday 9 November 2026. ACU is not accepting applications through this recruitment portal. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912156712082999~1/edit": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Assurance",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 Department: Assurance Unit Location: NSW,QLD,VIC Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a young and dynamic institution making a significant impact. Founded on the principles of Catholic social teaching, it aims to promote academic excellence, serve communities, and act as a catalyst for positive change. Ranked in the top two per cent of universities worldwide and in the top 10 Catholic universities, the university has seven campuses around Australia, a campus in Rome, Italy, and an online campus - ACU Online. ACU's Vision 2033 presents a strategy which allows students and staff to respond to the needs of a changing world while working to enable flourishing lives, foster thriving communities and forge an ethical future. Based in either Sydney, Melbourne, or Brisbane and reporting directly to the General Counsel and Chief Legal, Assurance and Governance Officer, the Associate Director, Assurance is responsible for strengthening ACU's assurance capability by leading a coordinated, risk-based program of assurance activities across enterprise risk management, compliance monitoring, internal audit and internal review; with oversight of institutional quality and regulatory readiness (including TEQSA). The role provides strategic advice, timely reporting and independent insight to support transparency, accountability and informed decision-making, including through reporting to the Vice-Chancellor's Management Committee (VCMC), the Audit & Risk Committee (and other governance committees as required) and the monitoring and validation of remediation actions. The Associate Director builds organisational capability and maturity in self-assurance practices, supports consistent evidence and documentation standards, and promotes continuous improvement across the university. We are seeking candidates with inclusive leadership skills and experience in a large, complex, and preferably regulated organisation. The successful candidate will be a highly collaborative and mission-led professional who will work with colleagues across other central service functions and the academic community to drive enterprise-wide transformation in Assurance and Risk. For a confidential discussion or to request the candidate information booklet, please contact Kate Robinson on +61 409 769 560 or at krobinson@robinsonfitzgerald.com.au or Janine Fitzgerald on +61 424 164 765 or at jfitzgerald@robinsonfitzgerald.com.au quoting reference RF0274. Applications can be sent to either or both of the above email addresses and will close on 11 November 2026. ACU is not accepting applications submitted through this recruitment portal. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912147452272599~1/edit": {
      "title": "National Manager, Payroll Services",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/11/2026 Department: Payroll Services Location: NSW,QLD Campus Location: Brisbane, Australia Job No: APTAV134376#003 Exceptional national payroll leadership opportunity to manage ACU's payroll function, provide expert advice and ensure compliance Lead a high performing team delivering crucial People & Culture and payroll services ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, fixed term 15 month opportunity with some hybrid flexibility working at North Sydney or Brisbane campus About the role: Operating within Payroll Services , the National Manager, Payroll Services operates in a complex industrial and regulatory environment and leads a team of payroll specialists delivering accurate and timely fortnightly payroll, workers compensation, superannuation, taxation and related third-party payment services for ACU nationally. Reporting to the Associate Director - Workforce Systems, Reporting & Payroll the position has responsibility for managing the end to end payroll function, providing expert advice on payroll related matters and ensuring ongoing compliance with relevant ACU policies and industrial, external regulatory, Federation and State Government legislative requirements. The National Manager, Payroll Services will drive high standards of performance within the Payroll Services team building a culture of continuous improvement and service excellence enabling timely resolution of all payroll queries and supporting effective stewardship of university resources. The National Manager, Payroll Services will have demonstrated experience in Aurion Payroll & HR Solutions, expertise in managing payroll systems and ability to manage a complex fortnightly payroll. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Steve Dobson, Associate Director - Workforce Systems, Payroll & Reporting at: steve.dobson@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $207,150 - $207,150 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $175,521 - $175,521 (pro rata) pa (HEW 10 Base 4), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 01-NOV-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. #LI-DNI Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912148671596499~1/edit": {
      "title": "Assistive Technology Specialist",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/11/2026 Department: Access and Disability Service Location: ACT,NSW,QLD,VIC Campus Location: Canberra, Australia | North Sydney, Australia | Brisbane, Australia | Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV101656#006 Provide specialist advice, training and implementation support in assistive technologies (AT) Play an integral role to enable equitable participation for students with disability. ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Part time, 28 hours per week, two year fixed term role at our Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney or Brisbane campus with some hybrid flexibility About the role: Operating within Access and Disability Service , the Assistive Technology Specialist provides specialist advice, training and implementation support in assistive technologies (AT) and accessibility tools to enable equitable participation for students with disability, health conditions and neurodivergence. In alignment with the Australian Disability Strategy 2021-2031 (AusDS), the position builds university capability by evaluating and recommending AT solutions, guiding coordinated implementation with relevant stakeholders and developing a sustainable suite of resources and training materials that strengthen ACU's in-house AT capability and aligns with relevant accessibility standards and legislative obligations. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Trevor Ianna, National Manager, Access and Disability Service at: trevor.ianna@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $128,699 - $139,238 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $108,751 - $117,657 (pro rata) pa (HEW 7), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 01-NOV-26 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. This position requires a Working with Children Check (WWCC) and/or Working with Vulnerable People Check (WWVP) (ACT only). Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912150569301999~1/edit": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, Program Delivery",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/11/2026 Department: PSH Education and Catholic Mission Location: NSW,VIC Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV101013#006 Lead the enterprise-wide implementation of ACU's Education and Student Success Plan (ESSP). Provide high-level strategic leadership and expert advice to senior executives, ESSP domain leads and co-leads. Drive exceptional student experience by translating ambition into impactful and future-focused delivery outcomes across six transformational domains. Full time, continuing role at our Melbourne or North Sydney campus with some hybrid flexibility. About the role: As Senior Manager, Program Delivery, you will: Lead the enterprise-wide implementation of ACU's Education and Student Success Plan (ESSP), providing high-level strategic leadership, expert advice and oversight to ensure ESSP priorities are translated into integrated strategies, sustainable operating models, and measurable organisational outcomes across the University. Drive complex, large-scale, cross-functional strategic initiatives that support ACU's Vision 2033 and advance the University's education, student success, and Catholic mission objectives. Work closely with senior executives, ESSP domain leads and co-leads, influencing direction, strengthening execution capability and addressing delivery risks to embed consistent approaches to planning, governance, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement. Lead complex strategic initiatives within the Professional Services Hub (PSH) Education and Catholic Mission Portfolios. Set delivery frameworks, coordinate multi-stakeholder implementation, resolve issues, and ensure outcomes are achieved where initiatives span multiple functional areas, involve significant change or require advanced design and delivery capability. Apply human-centred design, systems thinking and advanced program delivery expertise to shape how initiatives are designed and embedded in practice, contributing to measurable improvements in student outcomes and organisational effectiveness. Act as a steward of delivery discipline and strategic coherence, enabling ACU to realise the intent of its strategy in a consistent, scalable, and sustainable way in alignment with the university's Catholic mission and values. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Monica Chen, Associate Director Strategy & Operations - PSH Education and Catholic Mission at: monica.chen@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $187,558 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $158,738 (pro rata) pa (HEW 10 Base 1), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 01-NOV-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. This position requires a Working with Children Check (WWCC) and/or Working with Vulnerable People Check (WWVP) (ACT only). Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
