    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912148404903599~1/edit": {
      "title": "Future Students Coordinator NSW & ACT",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/11/2026 Department: Future Students Location: NSW Campus Location: Blacktown, Australia | North Sydney, Australia Job No: APTAV112940#009 Opportunity to support prospective students explore their study options, drive engagement and promote ACU's NSW & ACT campuses Work with a positive, dynamic team that celebrates successes and passionate about performance excellence ACU offers 17% superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, permanent opportunity with hybrid flexibility working at North Sydney or Blacktown campus About the role: Operating within Future Students , the Future Students Coordinator NSW & ACT is responsible for assisting the Future Students Lead to coordinate and drive recruitment activities that promote the university's North Sydney, Blacktown, Strathfield and Canberra campuses in local and regional areas as well as facilitating high quality applications from prospective students and supporting the wider Marketing team with national initiatives. Working closely with faculties and university stakeholders, the Future Students Coordinator will enhance recruitment opportunities and manage student recruitment communications and activities. The position maintains a thorough understanding of the breadth and depth of university courses, programs, campus amenities and student services available in NSW and ACT and delivers recruitment programs that communicates ACU's unique offering to prospective students to drive applications and enrolments. An important aspect of the role will be to develop and nurture relationships with university stakeholders, high school communities (Careers Advisers, teachers and Principals), community groups, local governments and councils, venues and external providers. The Future Students Coordinator may be required to work at any of the three ACU NSW campuses and some local and interstate travel to meet operational needs. Flexibility in working hours is needed to attend events and activities held outside standard business hours at offsite locations. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Carmen Di Lullo, Integrated Marketing Manager - Future Students at: Carmen.DiLullo@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $112,625 - $120,977 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $95,170 - $102,227 (pro rata) pa (HEW 6), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 05-NOV-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. This position requires a Working with Children Check (WWCC) and/or Working with