    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912148507767999~1/edit": {
      "title": "Graduations Officer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/11/2026 Department: Graduations and Protocol Location: NSW,QLD Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Brisbane, Australia Job No: APTAV135964#001 Exciting opportunity to combine planning, coordination and event management. Join a small, dedicated team that loves creating meaningful celebrations for our graduates. ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions. Full time, fixed term role from January - June 2027 at our Brisbane or North Sydney campus with some hybrid flexibility and interstate travel. About the role: Operating within Graduations and Protocol , the Graduations Officer is responsible for the student and staff registration components and other conferral and ceremonial functions for all ACU Graduation ceremonies within Australia. The annual graduation ceremonies are one of the University's foremost public events therefore the position plays an important role in enhancing the University's image. Graduation ceremonies are typically conducted each year at ACU locations across Australia, and attended by some 6,000 graduands and 14,000 guests. For full position details, refer to the position description. Interviews have been tentatively scheduled for Wednesday 11 November 2026. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Lauren O'Keeffe, National Manager, Graduations and Protocol at: lauren.okeeffe@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $116,410 - $125,049 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $98,367 - $105,667 (pro rata) pa (HEW 6), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Interviews have been tentatively scheduled for Wednesday 11 November 2026. Applications close: 05-NOV-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. This position requires a Working with Children Check (WWCC) and/or Working with Vulnerable People Check (WWVP) (ACT only). Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. 