    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912148577457099~1/edit": {
      "title": "Technology Support Officer (NSW)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/11/2026 Department: Service Operations Location: NSW Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia Job No: APTAV102359#004 Excellent opportunity to support the day to day functioning and management of technology and IT services for the ACU community Join a high performing, motivated national Service Operations team delivering exceptional customer experiences ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, permanent opportunity with some hybrid flexibility working at North Sydney campus About the role: Operating within Service Operations , the Technology Support Officer (NSW) will deliver client focused experiences using service management tools, processes and reporting to support ACU campuses nationally and audio-visual enabled spaces. Under leadership of the Service Operations Lead, the primary focus of the role is to remotely support the day to day functioning and management of technology and IT services used by staff, academics, students, internal stakeholders and university visitors as part of the ACU's Information Technology environment. This position requires highly effective communication skills to understand technical problems or requests and specialist technical knowledge and skills to triage and resolve service requests, provide advice and offer solutions. The Technology Support Officer is required to work rostered hours which may include afterhours and nominated weekends to ensure service requirements are being met. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Patrick Lui, Service Operations Lead - Service Operations at: patrick.lui@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $101,464 - $109,838 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary com