    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912143586717499~1/edit": {
      "title": "Team Leader",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Department: PSH Law & Business Location: NSW,VIC Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV133865#004 Oversee administrative operations for assigned schools within the FLB Professional Services Hub (PSH). ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions. Part time, 17.5 hours per week, fixed term role until October 2027 at our North Sydney campus with some hybrid flexibility. About the role: The Team Leader oversees administrative operations for assigned schools within the Faculty of Law and Business (FLB) Professional Services Hub (PSH), leading the assigned school operation teams in course and student administration, staffing, data analysis & reporting, continuous improvement initiatives, and communication with other PSH Team Leaders and Faculty operational staff. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Wendy Dimond, Director - PSH Law & Business and Theology & Philosophy at: wendy.dimond@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $128,699 - $139,238 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $108,751 - $117,657 (pro rata) pa (HEW 7), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Descri