    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912147371511099~1/edit": {
      "title": "Systems & Integration Engineer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Department: Application and Integration Services Location: VIC Campus Location: Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV132219#001 Excellent opportunity to analyse, document, develop and maintain the technical aspects of ACU's software integrations and improvements Work with high performing team supporting integrations of business critical systems ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, permanent opportunity with some hybrid flexibility working at Melbourne campus About the role: Operating within Application & Integration Services , the Systems & Integration Engineer is responsible for analysing, documenting, developing and maintaining technical aspects of ACU's software integrations, improvements and development. Working closely with internal stakeholders, end users, project team members and external vendors the position will develop actions or recommend solutions appropriate to university business requirements. Reporting to the Solution Architecture Lead Integration, the Systems & Integration Engineer will ensure the effective delivery, implementation and maintenance of new and existing integrations that support business critical systems. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Ravi Bhaskarla, Solution Architect Lead Integration - Application & Integration Services at: ravi.bhaskarla1@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $138,111 - $154,409 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $116,706 - $130,478 (pro rata) pa (HEW 8), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent t