      "description": "Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Department: Peter Faber Business School Location: NSW,VIC Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV103571#014 Provide academic leadership and disciplinary expertise to support the growth, quality, and ongoing enhancement of the Economics discipline. ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions. Full time, continuing role at our Melbourne or North Sydney campus with some hybrid flexibility, About the role: Operating within Peter Faber Business School , the Senior Lecturer/Associate Professor in Economics provides academic leadership and disciplinary expertise to support the growth, quality, and ongoing enhancement of Economics teaching, curriculum, research, and industry engagement within the Peter Faber Business School. The role contributes to the development and enhancement of the School's Economics curriculum, supporting the delivery of high-quality Economics subjects and programs, and advancing strategic priorities through curriculum innovation, program development, and the delivery of high-quality learning experiences across undergraduate and postgraduate offerings. The School particularly welcomes expertise in health economics, given ACU's strength in health. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Heather Summers, Executive & Project Officer- Peter Faber Business School at: eabusiness@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $184,462 - $200,262 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $156,092 - $169,597 (pro rata) pa (Senior Lecturer - Academic Level C), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading or total remuneration valued to $209,060 - $230,113 total rem (pro 