    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912143588927699~1/edit": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Speech Pathology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 Department: Speech Pathology (North Sydney) Location: NSW Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia Job No: APTAV102103#100 Outstanding Associate Professor opportunity to significantly influence learning and education in the discipline of Speech Pathology Join a highly recognised national school and work closely with colleagues to enhance the student experience ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, continuing opportunity working at North Sydney campus About the role: Operating within Speech Pathology (North Sydney) , the Associate Professor, Speech Pathology, a teaching and research focused role, will provide leadership, make outstanding and original contributions to learning, education, scholarship and research, and drive enhancement of the student experience at ACU in the discipline of Speech Pathology. The position will be responsible for course coordination and impact the development and implementation of the Bachelor of Speech Pathology course by providing theoretical and clinical teaching and research. Working collaboratively with the Head of School, Deputy Head of School, National Head of Discipline, Course Coordinators and other staff as required the Associate Professor will ensure that the delivery of the curriculum is comprehensively managed. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Erin Conway, Professor, Speech Pathology - School of Allied Health at: Erin.Conway@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $202,272 - $222,654 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $171,352 - $188,772 (pro rata) pa (Academic Level D), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superan