    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912148624881599~1/edit": {
      "title": "AskACU Centre Service Officer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/11/2026 Department: AskACU Centre - QLD/ACT Location: QLD Campus Location: Brisbane, Australia Job No: APTAV129152#003 Provide quality customer service support to current and prospective students. ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions. If you're passionate about helping others, thrive in a fast-paced environment, and want to make a real difference in a student's journey, then this is the role for you! Full time, continuing role at our Brisbane campus. About the role: Working as part of a national team, the AskACU Service Officer provides quality customer service support to current and prospective students and staff on a range of topics. Working in the AskACU Centre, the AskACU Service Officer (AskACU Centre) responds to enquiries by face-to-face, email, phone, live chat, and other enquiry-types as appropriate. The position-holder is responsible for case-management of enquiries and being the first point of call for the ACU Community. This position ensures students and staff receive a positive customer service experience on campus by resolving issues, providing relevant services and supporting high level enquiry management. For full position details, refer to the position description. Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Kirsty Krishna, Coordinator - AskACU Centres at: Kirsty.Krishna@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $104,877 - $113,049 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $88,621 - $95,940 (pro rata) pa (HEW 5), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commenceme